      "writtenOn": "2026-11-04T21:34:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Not introduced by this patch, but while reading this: is it safe for the worker in zram_deferred_prefetch() to access pf_ctl, which lives on the stack of zram_prefetch_slots()?\n\nWhat guarantees that the on-stack pf_ctl is still valid when zram_prefetch_dec_and_wake() calls wake_up()? wait_event() can return via its fast path as soon as num_inflight hits 0, without taking the\nwaitqueue lock, so wake_up() may touch a dead stack frame. The bio error path in zram_prefetch_read_endio() has the same issue.",
      "revId": "dbb8566694054c65eb36b06244217a7bdd4844f5",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
